1. Scope
--------
This licence covers the source code, documentation and other files in this repository that Ali Ben Mussa
("the owner") wrote. It does not cover third-party components. Section 5 explains them.

2. What you may do
------------------
You may, free of charge:

a. read and study the source code;
b. run the software on your own computer, or on a test server that you control, to evaluate it, review it or
   learn from it;
c. make changes for these purposes, and keep them private.

The organisers and judges of the Islamic AI Challenge 2026 may also use the software under the evaluation
licence in the challenge terms. Those terms apply to them in addition to this licence.

3. What you may not do without written permission
-------------------------------------------------
You need the owner's written permission to:

a. use the software, or any part of it, for a commercial purpose;
b. offer the software, or a service built on it, to other people as a hosted or online service;
c. publish, distribute, sell or sublicense the code, in its original form or as a modified version.

A short quotation of the code in a review, an article or a discussion is not a redistribution. Give the source.

To ask for permission, contact the owner through the repository.

4. Ownership
------------
The owner keeps all rights that this licence does not grant. Nothing in this licence transfers ownership.
Your changes do not give you rights in the owner's code.

